# Design Voice

> Creates a voice from a text description, with no reference audio. Pass the returned `voice_id` as `pipeline_config.tts_config.tts_voice_id` when you start a session.

> **Use the voice when you create a session**
>
> ```json theme={null}
> {
>   "pipeline_config": {
>     "tts_config": {
>       "tts_voice_id": "voice_8f2c1a4e"
>     }
>   }
> }
> ```
>
> Only the `tts_voice_id` is required: the service fills `tts_provider` / `tts_model_id` for that voice.

> **Is this the same as Clone Voice?**
>
> Both endpoints return a usable voice in the same shape. The difference is where the voice comes from:
>
> | | Clone Voice | Design Voice |
> | - | - | - |
> | Input | Reference audio (`file_id`) | Text description (`instruction`) |
> | You need to record audio first | Yes | No |
> | Extra response field | — | `preview_audio_url` |
> | Billing against `max_voices` | Yes | Yes, same quota |
>
> They share one voice quota, so a designed voice counts against the same `max_voices` limit as a cloned one.

> **Writing the instruction**
>
> The `instruction` describes the voice, not the content. Keep it concrete and about delivery:
>
> ```text wrap theme={null}
> A warm female narrator in her thirties, slightly husky, unhurried pace, gentle emphasis on the ends of sentences.
> ```

> **Preview audio**
>
> `preview_audio_url` is a permanent, unauthenticated WAV (mono, 16 kHz) you can play directly in an `<audio>` element or download.
>
> The field is **absent** when the preview could not be generated. A missing preview does **not** mean the voice failed — the voice is still usable for sessions. There is no status field to poll: the response itself means the voice is ready.

> **Errors**
>
> Error responses use the same `{code, message, data}` envelope; a non-zero `code` identifies the error.
>
> | Case | Error code |
> | - | - |
> | Missing `instruction` or `name` | `20003 missing required parameter` |
> | Missing `sample_text` for a language other than `zh` / `en` | `20003 missing required parameter` |
> | `instruction` or `sample_text` exceeds 1500 characters | `20004 invalid parameter` |
> | `name` exceeds 100 characters | `20004 invalid parameter` |
> | `language` is invalid | `20004 invalid parameter` |
> | The voice quota (`max_voices`) is reached (HTTP 403) | `30010 voice clone quota exceeded` |
> | The design provider call failed (HTTP 502) | `30007 voice clone provider failed` |
> | The API key is missing or invalid | `10001 missing api key` or `10003 invalid api key` |


## OpenAPI

````yaml streaming-avatar/api-references/openapi.json POST /v1/voices/design
openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: Vivix Streaming Avatar API
  version: 1.0.0
  description: REST endpoints for Streaming Avatar sessions, voices, and characters.
servers:
  - url: https://api.vivix.ai
security:
  - bearerAuth: []
paths:
  /v1/voices/design:
    post:
      summary: Design Voice
      description: >-
        Creates a voice from a text description, with no reference audio. Pass
        the returned `voice_id` as `pipeline_config.tts_config.tts_voice_id`
        when you start a session.
      operationId: designVoice
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              properties:
                instruction:
                  type: string
                  description: >-
                    Describes the voice to synthesize: timbre, age, speaking
                    style, pace. At most 1500 characters. Required.
                name:
                  type: string
                  description: Display name, at most 100 characters. Required.
                sample_text:
                  type: string
                  description: >-
                    Text the voice speaks in the generated preview. At most 1500
                    characters. Required when `language` is neither Chinese nor
                    English; optional for `zh` and `en`, where the service
                    supplies a default.
                language:
                  type: string
                  description: >-
                    Language of `sample_text`: `zh` (Chinese), `en` (English),
                    `fr` (French), `de` (German), `ja` (Japanese), `ko`
                    (Korean), `ru` (Russian), `pt` (Portuguese), `th` (Thai),
                    `id` (Indonesian), `vi` (Vietnamese), `it` (Italian), `es`
                    (Spanish), `ms` (Malay), `fil` (Filipino), `ar` (Arabic).
              required:
                - instruction
                - name
            example:
              instruction: A mature male news anchor with a deep, steady voice
              sample_text: Welcome to tonight's broadcast.
              language: zh
              name: Studio Anchor
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Success
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - code
                  - message
                  - data
                properties:
                  code:
                    type: integer
                    description: '`0` on success; any other value is an error code.'
                  message:
                    type: string
                    description: '`success`, or an English error description.'
                  data:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      voice_id:
                        type: string
                        description: >-
                          Voice id (shaped like `voice_…`). Pass it unchanged as
                          `tts_voice_id`.
                      name:
                        type: string
                        description: Display name.
                      language:
                        type: string
                        description: Language sent on create; empty string when omitted.
                      preview_audio_url:
                        type: string
                        description: >-
                          Public URL of the generated preview audio, playable
                          directly in an `<audio>` element. WAV (mono, 16 kHz).
                          Present only when the preview was generated; if it is
                          absent the voice is still usable.
                    required:
                      - voice_id
                      - name
                      - language
              example:
                code: 0
                message: success
                data:
                  voice_id: voice_8f2c1a4e-5d67-4b03-a9f1-2e6c7b0d5a94
                  name: Studio Anchor
                  language: zh
                  preview_audio_url: >-
                    https://static.vivi-x.ai/voice_preview/2026/10/13/8f2c1a4e5d674b03/a9f12e6c7b0d5a94.wav
components:
  securitySchemes:
    bearerAuth:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
      description: Your Vivix API key. Keep it on your server.

````

